@startuml credential-source-lifecycle
' Revision 2026-10-12: accepted review findings; Draft semantics, no renderer/qualification evidence.
title Credential source lifecycle - current per-home; source-policy v1/v2 targets; broker slices 0/1; SH2 and donor later
state "Resolve source metadata\nCaller-side Curator / curator-run\nuser-owned configuration" as Resolve
state "Migration inspect -> plan -> apply\nCurator manager; preserve credential bytes\nmarker/config revisions pending" as Migrate
state "Refused\nno other source, native login or mode fallback" as Refused
state "Per-home native source\nHarness owns native login/store/refresh\nisolation is a separate axis" as Native
state "Explicit API-key helper\nprotected curator-run bridge executes admitted helper\nClaude owns helper cache" as Helper
state "Qualified helper delivery\nprotected bridge returns bounded API key through private helper pipe\nsettings contain opaque reference only" as HelperDelivery
state "Node enrollment\nhuman supplies intentionally minted material\nCurator stores secret; never exports native login" as Enroll
state "Node available\nOS-user-owned metadata + 0600 secret / 0700 directory\nmacOS/Linux first file backend" as Node
state "Broker enrollment / binding\nswarma-credential-broker service UID owns store\nCodex: fresh broker-owned vendor enrollment" as Broker
state "Final executor validation\nagent-account curator-run first broker consumer\nnode: qualified final executor; donor supervisor later" as Validate
state "Qualified exec delivery\nClaude: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\nCodex slice 1: external token + account ID to app-server" as Inject
state "Known expired / auth failure\nno Claude setup-token refresh\nreport typed error; preserve uncertainty" as Expired
state "Human re-enroll / restart\nprovider-side revocation is a separate human action" as Recover
state "Local node revoked\nCurator deletes stored item, marks node, stops owner" as Revoked
[*] --> Resolve
Resolve --> Native : explicit per-home or truly absent entry in source-policy v1
Resolve --> Refused : missing entry in source-policy v2; failed/partial/unreadable state
Resolve --> Migrate : explicit adoption / mode change / v2 migration
Migrate --> Native : record explicit per-home for existing logged-in homes
Migrate --> Refused : metadata/lock/link conflict; preserve both stores
Migrate --> Resolve : approved non-secret configuration applied
Resolve --> Helper : explicit helper selection; API-key lane only
Resolve --> Enroll : explicit node selected, enrollment requested by human
Enroll --> Node : protected input; enrolled_at is not issued_at; expires_at may be unknown
Enroll --> Refused : forbidden native-login extraction / invalid source
Resolve --> Node : explicit node reference
Resolve --> Broker : explicit broker account; slice 0 Claude, slice 1 Codex
Node --> Validate : current generation; known expiry checked, unknown stays unknown
Broker --> Validate : caller plan -> ready dispatcher socket -> current revocation.check -> root launcher -> agent executor
Broker --> Refused : dispatcher absent/unready; revocation.check revoked/unavailable; restore fenced
Helper --> Refused : unauthorized helper, conflicting settings, bad/oversize output or timeout
Helper --> HelperDelivery : validated authorized helper; suppress raw stderr; bounded private output
HelperDelivery --> Helper : issuer rotation; new launch/cache retry; restart for immediate cutover
Native --> Native : same home; harness refresh or interactive re-login
Node --> Expired : known-expired metadata
Node --> Refused : absent node / unreadable or malformed store; never native fallback
Validate --> Refused : unsupported required extension/capability; wrong peer/account/profile/channel;
Validate --> Refused : changed binding/policy/executable; competing source; unqualified effective source/children
Validate --> Refused : broker unavailable / revoked grant or account / retired generation
Validate --> Inject : recheck destination binding; node protected lookup or broker-authorized lease
Inject --> Expired : Claude expiry/auth failure: no refresh or native fallback
Inject --> Inject : Codex slice 1: one live refresh writer across replacement; qualified prior-attempt/store recovery
Inject --> Refused : unknown writer/store/external rotation; no blind retry after child absence
Inject --> Refused : Codex renewal fails/deadline missed: turn fails; no fallback login
Expired --> Recover : human mints new token; atomic store replacement
Recover --> Node : restart affected sessions; already running child keeps old token until restart
Node --> Revoked : explicit local node revoke
Revoked --> Enroll : explicit new enrollment; local deletion is not vendor revocation
note right of Validate
  Caller-side curator-run composes; swarma-dispatcher admits/provisions/tracks;
  Unix-socket service from slice 0 uses broker connection/framing protections;
  fresh signed caller/generation checks; recovery/readiness precede admission.
  Requester signs orchestrator delegation after generation-bound key registration;
  dispatcher verifies/records, never signs; registration alone gives no spawn authority.
  Recursive provisioning stays refused until bootstrap publication/qualification.
  revocation.check is point-in-time evidence; final bind/lease/renewal checks remain.
  root swarma-user-launcher passes immutable plan; agent-account curator-run
  verifies/executes only, no profile resolution and no network except broker.
  SH2 swarma-session-runner shares launch library; donor executor later qualified.
  Broker owns accounts/bindings/leases; Codex slice 1 requires qualified containment,
  kill-and-confirm, durable intent/process evidence and home reload across replacement.
  Unknown external rotation requires unavailability/re-enrolment, no fallback.
  Later host_start uses durable tuple-bound host admission permit; dispatcher starts
  through claim/effect/root receipt; fresh channel/current epoch/readiness before delivery.
  Retirement: quiesce, declared-key cleanup, home deletion; export closed-schema
  service metadata only, without agent-controlled strings/names/links/bodies.
  Separate explicit operator home retention states confidentiality is not guaranteed.
  Plans/fragments/receipts contain metadata only; harness can read injected token.
end note
note bottom of Enroll
